# The Dockerfile copies only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md and src/ explicitly,
# so the build context stays small regardless. These rules are the second line of
# defence — and matter for the ad-hoc `docker build .` case.

# --- 1. VCS AND CI ---
.git
.github

# --- 2. PYTHON: ENVS, CACHES, BYTECODE ---
# Recreated inside the image by `uv sync`; never copied in.
.venv
venv
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc

# --- 3. BUILD AND COVERAGE OUTPUT ---
dist
build
htmlcov
.coverage

# --- 4. TESTS ---
# Kept out of the image — except the fixture app, which docker/target.Dockerfile
# packages as a manual scan target. The `!` lines must stay after `tests`.
tests
!tests/__init__.py
!tests/fixtures

# --- 5. DOCS, SPECS, AND THE WEB UI ---
# Not needed to run the engine or the API.
specs
docs
web
node_modules

# --- 6. SCAN ARTIFACTS, DATABASES, SECRETS ---
*.sarif
scan-*.json
scan-*.html
reports
webvigil.local.toml
.env
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- 7. EDITOR AND OS ---
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
